# Adamantan-1-ol + 10 CHCl3: XTB2 MD, spherical confinement
# FIXED: same issue as the DMSO input (Adamantanol_10DMSO_MD.inp) - this file
#   reused the Apixaban-scale placement (offset 12.78 Ang, Cell Sphere radius
#   14.0 centered on Apixaban's centroid) directly. For this structure,
#   Adamantanol's centroid is (31.744, -20.775, -0.589) with a max
#   atom-centroid distance of only 3.27 Ang (vs Apixaban's 9.03), so 4 atoms
#   ended up OUTSIDE the 14.0 Ang confinement sphere at t=0 (up to 14.52 Ang
#   from the sphere center). No atom-overlap clash was present (closest
#   CHCl3-Adamantanol contact was 8.02 Ang - if anything, solvent was placed
#   too far away), but those 4 outlying atoms would feel a large, unphysical
#   restoring force from the very first MD step.
#
# This version rebuilds the 10 CHCl3 placement for Adamantanol:
#   - Sphere/placement center = Adamantanol's own centroid for THIS geometry
#     (31.744, -20.775, -0.589).
#   - Each CHCl3 placed at offset 6.5 Ang from that centroid, along the same
#     12 directions used throughout this project, with the molecule rotated
#     so its bulk (the 3 Cl atoms) points radially outward.
#   - Cell Sphere radius reduced to 10.0 Ang (vs the old 14.0), sized for
#     CHCl3's own extent from its C atom (1.77 Ang) plus a safety margin.
# Checked: min CHCl3-Adamantanol atom distance = 2.83 Ang (no clash), max
#   atom distance from the sphere center = 7.28 Ang (safely inside the 10.0
#   Ang sphere).

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.744, -20.775, -0.589, 10.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Adamantanol_10CHCl3_XTB.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

* xyz 0 1
